  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dayton Peace Agreement (DPA) and Gender - BiH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commissioning a review on the impact of the Dayton Peace Agreement (DPA) for gender equality within Bosnia and Herzegovina. The findings will deepen understanding of the legacy impact this has had on women&#x2019;s exclusion from institutional processes and functions since the establishment of the DPA, as well as its social consequences. Looking forward, it will highlight the needs and priorities of women, and make an intellectual contribution to the wider evidence base regarding the importance of gender in peace processes and Transitional Justice.</narrative>
  </description>
